static.solution:
\mathbf{i}= \langle 1,0\rangle and \mathbf{j}= \langle 0,1\rangle, using vector algebra we have:
\begin{array}{rcl}
-4\mathbf{i} - 3\mathbf{j} \amp =\amp  -4\langle 1,0\rangle  - 3\langle 0,1\rangle = \langle -4,0\rangle +\langle 0,-3\rangle \\
\amp =\amp  \langle -4+0,0 - 3\rangle = -4\boldsymbol{i}-3\boldsymbol{j}
\end{array}
The length of the vector is:
\|-4\mathbf{i} - 3\mathbf{j}\| =\sqrt{(-4)^2+(-3)^2}=\sqrt{25}
We use vector algebra and the definition of the standard basis vector to compute the components of the vector -3\mathbf{i}+5\mathbf{j}:
\begin{array}{rcl}
-3\mathbf{i}+5\mathbf{j} \amp =\amp  -3\langle 1,0\rangle + 5\langle 0,1\rangle = \langle -3,0\rangle +\langle 0,5\rangle \\
\amp =\amp  \langle -3+0,0+5\rangle = -3\boldsymbol{i}+5\boldsymbol{j}
\end{array}
The length of this vector is:
\| -3\mathbf{i}+5\mathbf{j}\| =\sqrt{(-3)^2+{(5)}^2}=\sqrt{34}
We find the components of the vector -1\mathbf{i} - 2\mathbf{j}:
\begin{array}{rcl}
-1\mathbf{i} - 2\mathbf{j} \amp =\amp  -1\langle 1,0\rangle  - 2\langle 0,1\rangle = \langle -1,0\rangle +\langle 0,-2\rangle \\
\amp =\amp  \langle -1+0,0 - 2\rangle = -\boldsymbol{i}-2\boldsymbol{j}
\end{array}
The length of this vector is:
\| -1\mathbf{i} - 2\mathbf{j}\| =\sqrt{(-1)^2+{(-2)}^2}=\sqrt{5}
We find the components of the vector 2\mathbf{i} - 4\mathbf{j}, using vector algebra:
\begin{array}{rcl}
2\mathbf{i} - 4\mathbf{j} \amp =\amp  2\langle 1,0\rangle  - 4\langle 0,1\rangle = \langle 2,0\rangle +\langle 0,-4\rangle \\
\amp =\amp  \langle 2+0,0 - 4\rangle = 2\boldsymbol{i}-4\boldsymbol{j}
\end{array}
The length of this vector is
\| 2\mathbf{i} - 4\mathbf{j}\| =\sqrt{(2)^2+{(-4)}^2}=\sqrt{20}
